{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-41464","model_call":13,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3086"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q3086"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1103074658#3_2319984085","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3086","rank":3,"snippet":"what you should do differently. Without humility, we are wearing blinders that get in the way of improving and growing. - Bonnie Davis , Destination Up 2. It Proves You Don't Know It All A humble leader recognizes when he or she makes mistakes and recognizes that he or she doesn't know it all. Humility keeps you grounded in business and allows one to find the necessary resources, human or financial to improve the bottom line. - Dr. Venessa Marie Perry , Health Resource Solutions, LLC 3. It Creates Endless Possibilities Humility is a leader's recognition that we have might not always have the answers, but we are open to exploring possibilities. What any individual knows, is always limited to their experience and view of the world. As leaders, developing a sense of <cover>humility will provide you with new perspectives, stronger relationships, happier </cover>customers, and signification personal and professional growth. -\" , \"start_char\": 2060.000000 , \"title\": \"17 Reasons Humility Will Help You Get Ahead\" , \"url\": \"https://www.forbes.com/sites/forbescoachescouncil/2017/10/17/17-reasons-humility-will-help-you-get-ahead/\" }"},"time":16},"model_calls":13,"document_judgments":12,"relevance_3":6,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
