{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-41464","model_call":14,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3086"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q3086"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_1885067522#17_3828756984","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3086","rank":4,"snippet":"Joy Summary | FREE PDF | The Book of Joy Summary | FREE PDF | Lasting Happiness in a Changing World Who Should Read “The Book of Joy”? And Why? About Dalai Lama and Desmond Tutu “The Book of Joy PDF Summary” Key Lessons from “The Book of Joy” The Nature of Joy The Obstacles to Joy The Eight Pillars of Joy “The Book of Joy” Quotes Our Critical Review Learn with our well-curated library! \" , \"segment\": \"perspective, humility, humor, acceptance, forgiveness, gratitude, compassion, and generosity. 1. Perspective means that there are many different angles to look at a thing. Taking a pause and looking at a problem a bit more open-mindedly may make you much <cover>happier than you’ll ever thought possible. 2. Humility – </cover>be humble and modest. As John C. Maxwell says wittily: “ People with humility don’t think less of themselves; they just think of themselves less.” 3.\" , \"start_char\": 6280.000000 , \"title\": \"The Book of Joy PDF PDF Summary - Dalai Lama & Desmond Tutu\" , \"url\": \"https://blog.12min.com/the-book-of-joy-pdf/\" }"},"time":14},"model_calls":14,"document_judgments":13,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
