{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-41464","model_call":15,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3086"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q3086"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1103074658#4_2319986357","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3086","rank":5,"snippet":"To Be Vulnerable 17. It Earns You Admiration And Respect \" , \"segment\": \"Humility keeps you grounded in business and allows one to find the necessary resources, human or financial to improve the bottom line. - Dr. Venessa Marie Perry , Health Resource Solutions, LLC 3. It Creates Endless Possibilities Humility is a leader's recognition that we have might not always have the answers, but we are open to exploring possibilities. What any individual knows, is always limited to their experience and view of the world. As leaders, developing a sense of <cover>humility will provide you with new perspectives, stronger relationships, happier </cover>customers, and signification personal and professional growth. - Alan Trivedi , Trivedi Coaching & Consulting Group Forbes Coaches Council is an invitation-only community for leading business and career coaches. Do I qualify? 4. It Magnifies Your Strengths Being authentically humble humanizes a leader, strengthens trust, and builds confidence and loyalty among others. Humility is the trait that magnifies all other positive attributes.\" , \"start_char\": 2627.000000 , \"title\": \"17 Reasons Humility Will Help You Get Ahead\" , \"url\": \"https://www.forbes."},"time":15},"model_calls":15,"document_judgments":14,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
