{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-41464","model_call":19,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3088"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q3088"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_801831629#23_1447228390","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3088","rank":2,"snippet":"lead to greater mindfulness. That’s why the Stoics integrated daily practices of reflection – the day in review. Part 3: What Does a Stoic Look Like? The Classic Misconception – Stoics Are Unemotional The Stoics tried to use reason and training to not act out of feelings. So that they could respond with reason and virtue to whatever they felt. Domesticate your emotions, don’t pretend they don’t exist. The Stoic Love for Mankind And what if others do wrong? True Beauty Lies in Character The Ideal Stoic Personality – The Stoic Sage What Now? - The Stoicism Cheat Sheet \" , \"segment\": \"Includes good-heartedness, benevolence, public service, fair dealing. Courage or Fortitude: Includes bravery, perseverance, authenticity (honesty), confidence. Self-Discipline or Temperance: Includes orderliness, self-control, forgiveness, <cover>humility. Now, when you act according to these virtues, you progress towards the Good Life, </cover>or Eudaimonia, the ultimate goal of lif\" , \"start_char\": 9629.000000 , \"title\": \"What is Stoicism? A Definition & 10 Stoic Key Principles\" , \"url\": \"https://www.njlifehacks.com/what-is-stoicism-overview-definition-10-stoic-principles/\" }"},"time":15},"model_calls":19,"document_judgments":17,"relevance_3":8,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
