{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-41464","model_call":41,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3103"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q3103"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_1476400383#1_2377328112","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3103","rank":3,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_1476400383#1_2377328112\" , \"end_char\": 1493.000000 , \"headings\": \"The <cover>Importance of Humility in Life</cover>The Importance of Humility in Life The Importance of Humility in Leadership Lessons in Humility Famous Humble Leaders Living By Faith – free eBook \" , \"segment\": \"A famous way of describing humility is that “it’s not thinking less of yourself, but thinking of yourself less.” In his book In Humility: An Unlikely Biography of America’s Greatest Virtue, Dr. David Bobb says, “The power promised by humility is the power over oneself, in self-government. But humility’s strength is obscured by the age of arrogance in which we live”. In other words, humility requires enormous self knowledge, self control, and self esteem. For this reason, it is often paired with leadership. The Importance of Humility in Leadership To be an effective leader, humility is a very important characteristic. It combines several traits that help you ultimately connect to people, and earn their respect. Some think it’s the one defining trait that can make a leader effective. "},"time":9},"model_calls":41,"document_judgments":39,"relevance_3":15,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
