{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-41464","model_call":43,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"humble people\" (+ happier happiness \"well-being\" wellbeing) (+ relationships stress generosity))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"humble people\" (+ happier happiness \"well-being\" wellbeing) (+ relationships stress generosity))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_20_1541559733#5_3367595601","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3105","rank":1,"snippet":"1_doc_20_1541559733#5_3367595601\" , \"end_char\": 4403.000000 , \"headings\": \" Education Articles & More How Humility Will Make You the Greatest Person Ever It's so hard to be humble. Here are three tips for taming your ego. Why is humility good? Three tips for cultivating humility 1. Embrace your humanness 2. Practice mindfulness and self-compassion 3. Express gratitude About the Author Vicki Zakrzewski We believe happiness should be free. \" , \"segment\": \"For example, <cover>humble people handle stress more effectively and report higher levels of physical and mental well-being. </cover>They also show greater generosity, helpfulness, and gratitude —all things that can only serve to draw us closer to others. Three tips for cultivating humility Given what scientists have discovered about humility, it’s evident that cultivating this quality is not for the faint-hearted, nor does it appear overnight. Yet it would seem that one of the great rewards of humility is an inner freedom from having to protect those parts that we try to hide from ourselves and others. In other words, we develop a quiet, understanding, and compassionate heart. ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_20_1541559733#5_3367595601","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":71},"model_calls":43,"document_judgments":41,"relevance_3":16,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
